---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Why MelodyMind Reviews publishes sourced album criticism without numerical scores, comments, or embedded players."
>
  <article class="static-page reading-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Close listening, stated plainly.</h1>
    <p class="static-page__lead">
      MelodyMind Reviews asks how an album works, where its choices hold, and where they
      fail. A review is an argument, not a product description.
    </p>
    <h2>What readers get</h2>
    <p>
      Every piece has a named author, publication date, central thesis, concrete track
      examples, sources, and external listening links. The Review Map shows where the
      argument touches the record without reducing a track to a score.
    </p>
    <h2>What stays out</h2>
    <p>
      There are no numerical ratings, public user scores, comments, purchase prompts,
      embedded players, or sponsored placements. MelodyMind’s own releases are not
      presented as independent criticism.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/editorial-standards/">Read the complete editorial standards</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    padding-block: var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .static-page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .static-page h2 {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xl);
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .static-page__lead {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--quiet-ink);
  }
</style>
